# Confirmation that the empty-prompt image gen path on /api/generate-image
# refuses BEFORE token charge (PR #34 fix appears to hold at the route level).

$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/generate-image \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"prompt":""}'
{"error":"Validation failed","details":[{"code":"too_small","minimum":1,"type":"string","inclusive":true,"exact":false,"message":"String must contain at least 1 character(s)","path":["prompt"]}]}

$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/generate-image \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'
{"error":"Validation failed","details":[{"code":"invalid_type","expected":"string","received":"undefined","path":["prompt"],"message":"Required"}]}

# Validation runs BEFORE quotaCheck middleware (see image route:
#   router.post('/', requireAuth, validateBody(ImageGenerateSchema), quotaCheck('image'), handleGenerateImage)
# so an empty/missing prompt 400s without ever calling quotaCheck → no charge → no refund needed.

# Inside the handler the only empty-prompt branch (imageController.ts:99-103) calls
# `qc.reconcile({ skip: true })` — also safe.

# REGRESSION VERDICT: PR #34 image-gen-empty-failure → token refund flow appears intact.

# However: the actual `chat`-mode image tool is a different path. The chat tool
# (imageGeneration.ts callImageGenTool) does have try/catch around chargeImage
# in imageController.ts:111-127 — this does charge in advance and refund on
# post-processing failure. Verified by code review only — could not trigger
# the Azure outage in QA.
